        {
          "kicker": "Costly scrum",
          "heading": "Fiji's late scrum penalty lets Tommaso Allan kick Italy to 23-21 win",
          "body": "Kitione Salawa had put Jake White's side ahead for the first time in Friday's 11th-place final at Twickenham, the No. 8's 55th-minute try and Caleb Muntz's third conversion making it 21-20 after Italy had led 17-0. The infringement came on the edge of Fiji's 22 with 13 minutes left; Allan, perfect with all five goal kicks, made no mistake. Fiji outscored the Azzurri three tries to two, a week after beating them 21-16 in Udine, but finish the Nations Championship 11th of 12."
