      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's rest",
          "heading": "Warburton hails Borthwick's 'stroke of genius' in resting Maro Itoje in July",
          "body": "Writing in The Times, the former Lions captain credited Borthwick with suggesting the break that kept Itoje out of July's Southern Series Tests against South Africa, Fiji and Argentina. The 32-year-old lock has been 'on fire this autumn,' Warburton argued. He cited Itoje's 49 ruck entries in last Saturday's 37-12 win over the All Blacks, with Ollie Chessum next on 31. He also pointed to a team-high 19 tackles in 63 minutes against Japan. Itoje captains England again in today's third-place play-off at Twickenham."
        },
